[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Client interoperability

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SFTP-042
STATUS: Active
TITLE: OpenSSH sftp client
STATEMENT: >>>
The server shall interoperate with the OpenSSH ``sftp`` client in batch mode with a pinned host key: login with an Ed25519 or ECDSA identity, put, get, ls -l, mkdir, rename, rm and rmdir, under every supported cipher, MAC and key exchange, and with forced rekeying.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- OpenSshSftpTests.PutAndGet_RoundTripThroughMemory
- OpenSshSftpTests.EveryCipherMacAndKeyExchange_Works
- OpenSshSftpTests.LargeTransfer_SurvivesRekeyingAndFragmentation
- OpenSshSftpTests.DirectoryFileSystem_UploadThenAtomicRename_LikeAnUploadJob
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
These tests skip when ``sftp`` and ``ssh-keygen`` are not on PATH, except on CI where they fail instead.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SFTP-043
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Client-visible failures
STATEMENT: >>>
Failures injected or produced by the server shall reach the OpenSSH client as the corresponding error: an injected FAILURE fails the transfer, PERMISSION_DENIED prints "Permission denied" for that file only, a wrong host key is refused before authentication, and an aborted connection fails the client while the server records no error.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- OpenSshSftpTests.FailNext_FailsOneUpload_ThenTheRetrySucceeds
- OpenSshSftpTests.PermissionDenied_FromFailAlways_IsReportedPerFile
- OpenSshSftpTests.PinnedHostKey_Mismatch_IsRefusedByTheClient
- OpenSshSftpTests.ConnectionDroppedMidUpload_ClientFails_ServerStaysHealthy
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SFTP-044
STATUS: Active
TITLE: SSH.NET client
STATEMENT: >>>
The server shall interoperate with SSH.NET for ECDSA key and password logins, host key fingerprint checks, upload with posix-rename, directory listing, download and delete.
<<<
VERIFIED_BY: >>>
- SftpExample.Publishes_ViaPartialFileThenAtomicRename
- SftpExample.PasswordLogin_WithSshNet
- SftpExample.CollectInbox_DownloadsThenDeletes
- SftpExample.ImpostorHost_IsRefusedBeforeAnyCredentialsAreSent
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Review decisions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ITS-SSH-046
STATUS: Rejected
TITLE: ssh-rsa (SHA-1) signatures opt-in only
STATEMENT: >>>
SHA-1 ``ssh-rsa`` user authentication signatures shall be accepted only when enabled by an explicit server option.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
SHA-1 ssh-rsa is accepted only when the client's own request names ssh-rsa, so there is no downgrade: a client that can use rsa-sha2-256 or rsa-sha2-512 (advertised in server-sig-algs) does so, and the signature algorithm must match the one the request declared. Making it opt-in would break old clients the fake exists to test.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Current behaviour is specified by ITS-SSH-005 and ITS-SSH-008. The server never signs with SHA-1 ssh-rsa itself (ITS-SSH-009).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ITS-SSH-008

[[/SECTION]]
